{
  "description": "Every tracked dependency lockfile or manifest that security-scan.yml's osv-scanner job scans. A lockfile entry without a parser lets OSV-Scanner infer it from the file name; parser names the OSV-Scanner v2 extractor for names it cannot infer (--lockfile=<parser>:<path>). A covered_by_lockfile entry is a manifest OSV-Scanner v2.6.0 has no source extractor for; its sibling lockfile is scanned instead. A dependency_free entry is a package.json that declares no dependency and has no lockfile beside it, so nothing is scanned for it; it needs a reason and an evidence path. An excluded entry is a tracked lockfile deliberately left out of the scan; it needs a reason and an evidence path, and a deliberately vulnerable test fixture or captured evidence lock that is not a live input qualifies. A lockfile entry that names a config is scanned in an invocation of its own under that config alone (an explicit --config applies to every input of one invocation), and every other entry together under .github/osv-scanner.toml; the tests bind each such config to its one lock. tests/test_osv_lockfile_coverage.py fails when a tracked lockfile or manifest is in none of the four lists.",
